**`provenance.py`'s A24 check had six bugs across three cycles and its own self-test passed over every one.** The self-test used a year-2020 artifact, which fails on the HEAD floor alone — a control exercising one of two mechanisms was silently reporting on both. So "patch a source, don't commit it, run the binary built before the patch" — the `fuelrun.v2.*` case that burned both lanes — was undetectable for the whole project.

